## Duplicadas O Superpuestas

| Cluster | Senales | Observacion | Recomendacion |
|---|---|---|---|
| Confidence | `confidence`, `confidence_score`, `confidence_label`, `confidence_reasons`, `confidence_risk_flags` | `confidence` es alias legacy de `confidence_label`. | Usar `confidence_score` + `confidence_label`; mantener `confidence` solo compatibilidad. |
| Comparable count | `comparable_count`, `comparables_used`, `n_comparables`, `comparables_count` | Mismo concepto en Valuation, Radar, beta metrics y engine results. | Canonico publico: `comparable_count`; por motor: `engine_results[].comparables_count`. |
| Score | `score`, `ranking_score`, `scores.overall` | Radar score y Risk Report score no miden lo mismo. | Renombrar conceptualmente a `opportunity_score` vs `risk_report_score`/`investment_score`. |
| Microzona | `geo_signals`, `geo_microzone_tokens`, `same_microzone_ratio`, `geographic_microzone.microzone_id` | Microzona textual se usa; geografica es audit/read-only. | Separar `textual_microzone` y `geographic_microzone`. |
| Price provenance | `price_uf_source`, `price_uf_confidence`, `price_recovery_method`, `price_display_basis`, `price_basis_used`, `price_data_quality` | Mezcla decision de producto con provenance tecnica. | Exponer `price_quality_label`; esconder raw provenance en modo usuario. |
| Warning flags | `warnings`, `comparable_quality_flags`, `reliability_warnings`, `confidence_risk_flags`, `beta_scope_flags`, `risk_flags` | Una misma debilidad se repite en varios arrays. | Crear `evidence_flags` normalizado con `code`, `source`, `severity`, `category`. |
| Estimated value aliases | `estimated_price_uf`, `estimated_value_uf`, `market_price`, `estimate_uf` | Alias por endpoint/adaptador. | Canonico conceptual: `avm_estimated_value`. |
| Surface | `surface.stats`, `surface_adjustment_*` | Ajuste visible, stats no visibles. | Traducir a senal de producto: “soporte local de mercado”, no `weight/reason`. |

## Senales Visibles Que Son Tecnicas

Estas deberian ocultarse, traducirse o agruparse antes de entrar a Investment Intelligence / Listing Opportunity:

- `confidence` legacy alias si ya existe `confidence_label`.
- Codigos crudos en `warnings`.
- `confidence_risk_flags`, `comparable_quality_flags`, `beta_scope_flags`, `risk_flags`.
- `beta_scope_status`, `beta_scope_message` con vocabulario beta interno.
- `surface_adjustment_applied`, `surface_adjustment_weight`, `surface_adjustment_reason`.
- `engine_results.*`: `engine_name`, `engine_version`, `role`, `status`, `safe_error_message`.
- `consensus_method`, `engine_weights`, `selected_engine_names`.
- `price_uf_source`, `price_uf_confidence`, `price_recovery_method`.
- `price_display_basis`, `price_basis_used`, `price_data_quality`, `saved_price_basis`.
- `uf_rate_used_for_display`, `uf_rate_source`, `uf_rate_is_fallback`.
- `price_history.is_artifact`, `price_history.artifact_reason`, `price_history.change_basis`.
- `listing_url_lookup.status` y `listing_url_lookup.warnings` como codigos raw.

## Recomendacion De Arquitectura Conceptual

Proponer una capa intermedia `SignalRegistry`/`ReportSignalSet` antes de los reportes:

- `valuation_quality`: confidence, comparable_count, dispersion, geo quality, comparable quality, beta scope.
- `market_context`: comuna, property_type, area bucket, microzone, segment depth, price surface context.
- `listing_opportunity`: published price, discount, watchlist, price history, price-drop events, listing freshness.
- `technical_provenance`: raw warnings, engine diagnostics, price provenance, geocode provenance, cache/debug.

Los reportes deberian consumir una forma normalizada:

```json
{
  "code": "price_per_m2_dispersion",
  "label": "Dispersion de comparables",
  "category": "Valuation Quality",
  "severity": "medium",
  "value": 62.5,
  "unit": "pct",
  "availability": "hoy",
  "source": "domain.valuation.comparable_quality"
}
```

Esto permite construir:

- `Investment Score`: solo B + C + A resumidas, sin D.
- `Risk Report`: A + C + B, con D traducida a etiquetas humanas.
- `Investment Intelligence Report`: B dominante, A como confiabilidad.
- `Listing Opportunity Report`: C dominante, A como soporte y B como contexto.

